## Problem

The chart loading functionality was experiencing 30-second timeouts on initial page load, even though the backend API endpoints were working correctly and chart files were already generated. Users would see "為 TWD-HKD 生成圖表時發生超時" (timeout error) instead of the expected charts.

## Root Cause

The `loadChart()` function in `currency_manager.js` was missing the direct chart API fetch logic. Instead of first attempting to retrieve existing charts via `/api/chart`, it was immediately falling back to the Server-Sent Events (SSE) pregeneration mode, which would timeout when charts were already available.

## Solution

Added the missing direct chart API fetch logic to `currency_manager.js`:

```javascript
// 先嘗試直接獲取圖表，如果失敗則使用預生成模式
try {
  const chartResponse = await fetch(`/api/chart?period=${period}&buy_currency=${fromCurrency}&sell_currency=${toCurrency}`);
  if (chartResponse.ok) {
    const chartData = await chartResponse.json();
    if (chartData.chart_url) {
      // 直接渲染圖表
      if (this.deps.renderChart) {
        this.deps.renderChart(chartData.chart_url, chartData.stats, fromCurrency, toCurrency, period);
      }
      // 更新前端快取和UI
      // ...
      return; // 直接返回，不需要預生成
    }
  }
} catch (error) {
  console.warn('直接獲取圖表失敗，將使用預生成模式:', error);
}
```

This implementation:
1. **Tries direct API fetch first**: Attempts to get existing charts immediately
2. **Updates frontend cache**: Successful responses are cached for faster subsequent loads  
3. **Graceful fallback**: If direct fetch fails, falls back to the existing SSE pregeneration mode
4. **Proper error handling**: Logs warnings and continues with fallback rather than failing

## Testing

- ✅ All chart periods (7d, 30d, 90d, 180d) load instantly without timeout
- ✅ Chart statistics display correctly (min/max/avg rates, data points, date ranges)
- ✅ Period switching works seamlessly
- ✅ Currency swapping maintains proper functionality
- ✅ Error handling works for unsupported currency pairs
- ✅ Backend API endpoints respond correctly (`/api/chart`, `/api/latest_rate`, `/api/pregenerate_charts`)

Added `test_chart_loading.py` script to verify all functionality programmatically.

## Impact

This fix eliminates the frustrating 30-second loading delays and provides users with immediate chart visualization, significantly improving the user experience while maintaining backward compatibility with the existing SSE-based pregeneration system.

